<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">Argentine Confederation</h1><p class="st-meta">1831 CE – 1861 CE · capital Buenos Aires</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The loose union of Argentine provinces dominated by Juan Manuel de Rosas, which gave Argentina its 1853 constitution before Buenos Aires reunited the nation.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-pact">Federal Pact</a> of 1831 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santa-fe-argentina">Santa Fe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/entre-rios-province">Entre Ríos</a>, later joined by the other provinces after the defeat of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/unitarian-league">Unitarian League</a>, created the Argentine Confederation. There was no national government; the governor of Buenos Aires conducted foreign relations on behalf of the provinces.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-manuel-de-rosas">Juan Manuel de Rosas</a>, governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> from 1829 to 1832 and from 1835 to 1852 with total public power, dominated the confederation. His police, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-mazorca">Mazorca</a>, terrorised Unitarian opponents. He resisted an Anglo-French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naval-blockade">blockade</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">River Plate</a> from 1845 to 1850. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justo-jose-de-urquiza">Justo José de Urquiza</a> defeated him at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-caseros">Caseros</a> in 1852, a congress adopted the Constitution of 1853, still in force, and the government sat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parana-entre-rios">Paraná</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> rejected the constitution and formed the separate <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-buenos-aires">State of Buenos Aires</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bartolome-mitre">Bartolomé Mitre's</a> victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-pavon">Pavón</a> in 1861, the nation reunited as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/argentine-republic">Argentine Republic</a>. The Constitution of 1853 remains the basis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina's</a> present constitution.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/argentine-confederation.jpg" alt="Argentine Confederation" width="320" height="207"><figcaption>Image: Guilherme Paula · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Argentina_(1840).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1831 CE – 1861 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Buenos Aires</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Juan Manuel de Rosas, Justo José de Urquiza, Santiago Derqui</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/argentina">Argentina</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Confederación Argentina</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1846&amp;focus=argentine-confederation" aria-label="Argentine Confederation on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="3120 3333 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Argentine Confederation lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3440 3589L3517 3686M3440 3589L3343 3578M3440 3589L3517 3686M3440 3589L3517 3686"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3517 3686h0M3343 3578h0M3517 3686h0M3517 3686h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3440 3589h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3440 3589h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1846&amp;focus=argentine-confederation">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
